;; pyi's divergences from CPython 3.14.10 over Lib/test (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md §7-§8, "As built: PY7 (the check)";
;; GR10's format, as test/goi/divergences.edn and test/java/divergences.edn): the classes every test method of bin/pyi
;; check that does not run as CPython runs it falls into, each with its title, :kind (:design, by design; :deferred, an
;; owner's work remains), :owner (the milestone or family whose files it waits on), :why, :decided (where), :match (the
;; regexes that find the method's "RESULT REASON", test/python/libtest_judge.ae's line: "import MESSAGE", "stopped-in
;; MESSAGE", "crash MESSAGE", "not-run", or pyi's "OUTCOME REASON") and :tests (the methods named, "MODULE/TEST-ID": those
;; whose line no pattern of the class finds). A method's class is the first class of this vector that names it in
;; :tests or one of whose :match finds its line (test/reap/main.ae's, test/cover/classes.ae's and java.check's rule).
;; The record of the check, every method's result, is test/python/check-lib-test-linux-amd64.edn (bin/pyi check
;; --record); bin/pyi divergences classifies it. Replaces test/python/lib-test-known.edn (queue 201, PY7: its :classes
;; are these, in its writer's order, alphabetical, the classes added since after them; its :methods those that no pattern
;; of their class finds, in :tests).
;; A class with :verdict :own (queue 234) is the own verdict's alone (test/python/libtest_judge.ae --verdict own, the
;; default): the recorded-run judge (--verdict ref, the oracle tier's) leaves it out.
;; Hand-maintained: no tool writes it. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :ast-objects
  :title "_ast's object model's rest: test_pickling's time"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "PY8 (the speed)"
  :why "Since 202c (queue 202) compile() of an AST object is converted and validated as CPython's (obj2ast, Python/ast.c's _PyAST_Validate), ast.parse(optimize=...) preprocessed (ast_preprocess.c), the node constructors, __replace__ and __reduce__ follow 3.14's rules (go/arbace/py/builtins_ast*.go); since queue 211 str constants are interned (intern_constants), b'' is one object and ast.parse applies the int digits limit; since queue 250 a ** keyword that is no str reaches a node class's __init__ and a node's __replace__ as the kwargs dict (kwDictCall: ast_type_init's == against the fields, its DeprecationWarning and setattr's TypeError, ast_type_replace's refusal by the key's repr): test_ast 206 of 217 equal on the VM. Left: test_pickling can pass its 300 s limit (every exec_tests tree pickled at protocols 0-5: it passed on the VM in queue 211's run, timed out in 250's). The patterns stay for the methods the VM did not sample"
  :decided "survey §6.6, PYS4; the user, 2026-11-03 (PY9 beside PY6); queue 201, PY9's finding 1; queue 202, 202c (the validator, the constructors, optimize: narrowed to the rest); queue 211 (interned constants, b'', the digits limit: narrowed; the AST cycle moved to :finalization-collect); queue 250 (the non-str keywords: narrowed; test_exceptions' two offset tests pass since before 250)"
  :match [#"^failure <class 'code'> != <class 'ast\.Module'>" #"compile\(\) arg 1 must be a string, bytes or AST object" #"'code' object has no attribute 'body'"]
  :tests ["test_ast/test.test_ast.test_ast.CopyTests.test_pickling"]}
 {:id :buffer-exports
  :title "buffer exports: a bytearray's not counted; a resize after a dropped view under goi or past the budget"
  :kind :deferred
  :owner "PY7 (queue 249)"
  :why "since queue 249 (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 249\") an array counts its exports (arraymodule.c's ob_exports: memoryview's managed buffer, released by release(), the context manager or the view's finalization; a refused resize asks Go's collector first whether the views died), so test_array's refusals are CPython's. Left: a bytearray counts none by default (PYI_BYTEARRAY_EXPORTS=1 counts: _pyio, pyi's io, resizes bytearrays it has just made temporary views of, FileIO.readall's, so every file read would ask the collector, and under goi a view goi's registers keep failed an import), so test_bytes' and test_memoryio's BufferError tests are here; past the collections' budget a resize is allowed; under goi a dropped view still in goi's registers refuses a resize CPython allows. Queue 473: test_buffer's test_memoryview_release (by name): `del nd` of a C consumer (_testbuffer's ndarray over a memoryview) does not release its Py_buffer at once (pyi counts no references: ndarray_dealloc runs when Go collects it), so the view's release() right after still finds its export (BufferError: memoryview has 1 exported buffer). Queue 475 (473-4 (a)), confirmed with PEP 688's slots ported: test_buffer's test_release_buffer_with_exception_set (b.extend(A()) must refuse the resize while memoryview(b) holds b) and test_release_saves_reference_no_subclassing (ba.clear() must refuse while the view __release_buffer__ kept holds ba) need a bytearray's exports counted; test_memoryview_release needs del's reference counts"
  :decided "survey §6.5, PYS9; PY6d's report (queue 200); queue 249; queue 475 (the three test_buffer rows confirmed)"
  :match [#"^failure BufferError not raised"]
  :tests ["test_buffer/test.test_buffer.TestBufferProtocol.test_memoryview_release"]}
 {:id :builtin-modules
  :title "pyi's C modules are built in"
  :kind :design
  :owner "none (by design)"
  :why "CPython on Alpine has zlib, math and the other C modules as lib-dynload extensions; pyi has no extension loader, so they are built in (sys.builtin_module_names names them) and a test that skips for a built-in module skips here"
  :decided "PY6-core round 3's Low (sys.builtin_module_names from the modules made); queue 200"
  :match [#"is a builtin module"]}
 {:id :c-accelerators
  :title "the C accelerators of pickle, json, decimal and datetime"
  :kind :design
  :owner "none (by design)"
  :why "since queue 227 (the user's decision on its DECISION (a), 2026-11-07) a thin _pickle exists: PickleBuffer, its other names pickle's pure twin by a module __getattr__. So test_pickle's C classes run on the pure Pickler: a pass among them says nothing about a C pickler, and the methods listed here that fail ask what only _pickle.c does (a C function not binding in a class body, its memo proxies and re-entrancy checks, its exact messages). pyi runs pickle, json, decimal and datetime as their pure-Python twins (survey §6.6, PYS11, E8): _pickle, _json, _decimal and _datetime are absent, so the tests of the C variants (test_pickle's C* classes, test_json's CTest, test_decimal's C classes and \"requires C version\" skips, test_datetime's _Fast classes) are absent or skip where CPython runs them; _decimal and _datetime stay absent by the user's decision (2026-11-04, PY6g's DECISION 1); inspect's signature of pickle.Pickler is the pure Pickler's (fix_imports keyword-only, where _pickle's text signature has none: test_signature_on_builtin_class; queue 278) Queue 290: test_inspect's test_excluding_predicates asks ismemberdescriptor(datetime.timedelta.days), a member of _datetime's timedelta, a property of _pydatetime's (it failed earlier, on ismethodwrapper, until method-wrapper came)."
  :decided "survey §6.6, PYS11; PY6d's and PY6g's reports (queue 200); the user, 2026-11-04: _decimal and _datetime stay absent, their C-variant tests classed by design (PY6g's DECISION 1); py-design-1122 (2026-11-21): _functools' reduce and cmp_to_key are _functoolsmodule.c's (built-in functions and functools.KeyWrapper), so a C class's attribute no longer binds as a method; _hmac (hmacmodule.c over Go's crypto) and _uuid (libuuid's generate_time_safe) exist"
  :match [#"requires _pickle" #"requires _json" #"No module named '_pickle'" #"No module named '_json'" #"requires C version" #"_decimal" #"_datetime" #"'NoneType' object has no attribute 'JSONDecodeError'"]
  :tests ["test_annotationlib/test.test_annotationlib.TestTypeRepr.test_type_repr"
