 {:id :finalization
  :title "finalization at reference counting's moment: __del__, weak references and ResourceWarning with no gc.collect() between"
  :kind :design
  :owner "none (by design: PYS9 (a); :finalization-collect is the runtime's finalizer queue)"
  :why "pyi's objects are Go's, collected by Go's collector: __del__ and weakref callbacks do not run when the last reference goes (an object a frame or exception held is still alive after gc_collect), the unraisable hook is not called from them; survey §6.5 (PYS9): a class measured at PY7; the test looks right after the last reference goes, with no gc.collect() (CPython's reference counting frees at once; PyPy's tests mark such checks cpython_only or call gc_collect): only counting (PYS9 (b), or (c) for the types concerned) has the timing. Measured at PY7 (queue 201): 47 of the families' 97 finalization methods, about 0.3% of their 14,132; statically 226 methods of all Lib/test use weak references, __del__, getrefcount or ResourceWarning without gc.collect (174 with it, 31 cpython_only). Since queue 222 a DELETE_FAST of a tracked object collects at once (finalize.go's finDeleted, bounded to a tenth of the wall time): the methods it serves pass compiled (:finalization-goi); rebinding (o = None), a frame's return, a container's item deleted and an iterator dropped still wait for the next collection (the survey's \"As built: 222\", the cost of a check on every store and return); since queue 274 the C API's watchers' DEALLOCATED and DESTROY events (dict, code and function watchers, _testcapi's watchers.c): no event when the last reference goes, and PyCode_NewEmpty's compile and code.replace make two code objects where CPython's makes one; night 12's run (queue 278): multiprocessing.heap's blocks freed by their Finalize when the last reference goes (test_heap: a block deleted from the list is not freed, the free and occupied sizes do not add up), and the executor's semaphores still registered with the resource tracker when test_init's FailingInitializerResourcesTest stops it (their Finalize not run: the tracker exits 1, leaked objects); queue 281: test_monitoring's test_generator_with_line (the last LINE event is CPython's close of the yield-from generator b at its last