 {:id :finalization-cycle
  :title "a cycle through an object with a finalizer: never freed, its __del__ never run, its weak references never cleared"
  :kind :design
  :owner "none (by design: PYS9 (a), queue 218)"
  :why "since queue 222 (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 222\") gc.collect() finds the cycles through instances, lists, tuples and dictionaries that hold a tracked object (CPython's gc_collect_main with Go's collector as the oracle of outside references: PEP 442's order, resurrection, gc.garbage under DEBUG_SAVEALL), and those methods pass compiled (:finalization-goi). These are what it cannot find soundly: a cycle through a class (its MRO holds it), a function, a cell, a frame or a generator, whose references are typed Go fields that cannot be hidden from Go's collector, or through an instance whose __dict__ was handed out; a weak reference inside the trash (CPython calls no callback for it: pyi's are held by their referent's record, :weakref-list); and the count of cyclic garbage with no finalizer and no weak reference (test_gc's test_list, test_dict and the rest: Go frees it untracked, so gc.collect() cannot count it). Before 222: the finalizer queue (queue 218) rests on Go's finalizers, and Go never frees a cycle that reaches an object with a finalizer from itself (runtime.SetFinalizer's documented rule): a tracked object (weakly referenced, or with a __del__) in a reference cycle stays alive, as CPython 2's uncollectable cycles did, without gc.garbage. Every class is in a cycle (its MRO holds it), so are a test's self-referencing instances, RefCycle, an AST node and its child, a dict view held by its key; PEP 442's cyclic resurrection and gc.collect's count of a cycle's objects follow. Only a collector of pyi's own over Python objects (roots: every frame, module and Go-held object) could find them. Queue 259 (read, the probable cause: their cycles run through an iterator's or a cache wrapper's Go-typed fields; sampled on goi, not compiled): test_set's and test_deque's test_container_iterator (gc.collect(), 'Cycle was not collected'), test_functools' test_lru_cache_weakrefable and test_method_no_reference_loops; test_dataclasses' test_original_class_is_gced (a cycle through a class) (queue 259's third sample of never-run lib-test-all modules, the VM at 6ee13e5ae, 2026-11-10)"
  :decided "queue 218 (doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"Design: 218\"); queue 222 (narrowed: the cycles through instances and containers found); the user, 2026-11-23 (proposal H): test_gc's twelve counts of cyclic garbage moved to :gc-cycle-count, n/a; the rest stays by design"
